anon wrote:
> My 9th level wizard just got swallowed again by an energy vortex, which
> took his HP down from 40-something to 27. What would be the best way to
> deal with this?

Energy Vortices are (I think) the most dangerous vortex type short of
air elementals, because not only does hitting with metal weapons shock
you, can they destroy items as well.

First, try teleporting out of there if you have the means.  Killing it
from a distance is a much better option than doing it from an adjacent
square, or from inside it.

A wand of digging works great with physical swallowers like Purple
Worms or Juiblex, but I don't think it works with vortices.  I think
zapping a wand of Slow Monster will disrupt it and allow you to escape,
although it could probably just engulf you again if you don't get away
after that.  Zapping wands and spells from inside is cool in that
you'll never miss.

Do you have any non-metal weapons to use?  If you hit it with a metal
weapon, you'll probably get an extra shock.  Unfortunately you probably
won't be above Unskilled or Restricted in something non-metal if you
haven't been using it regularly.  A quarterstaff of a unicorn horn
could be good for a last resort, however.

Remember prayer if your HPs get low.  You can get healing as the result
of a prayer if your hit points get below five or 1/7 your maximum,
whichever is greater.

